00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:11.530
administered to a patient in the
hospital, one saline solution contains 0.

00:20:11.590 --> 00:20:14.680
898 grams of sodium chloride.

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:20.629
In 525 milliliters of
solution, what is the molarity?

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:24.050
So from earlier, it was moles over liters.

00:20:24.370 --> 00:20:26.210
So and that's the most
important thing to remember.

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:33.169
Remember big M is moles over liters, which
is going to be used a lot in this course.

00:20:34.200 --> 00:20:37.990
So if we are to use this, the
first thing we need to do is

00:20:37.990 --> 00:20:40.840
convert our moles to liters.

00:20:41.889 --> 00:20:47.520
So what we have is grams of NaCl, and
I'm going to convert that to molarity.

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:52.040
So by using the molar mass of NaCl.

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:55.570
So the molar mass of NaCl is 58.

00:20:55.610 --> 00:20:56.370
44.

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:58.660
So let's write that down.

00:20:58.660 --> 00:21:00.179
So 58.

00:21:00.180 --> 00:21:01.610
44 grams.

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:05.320
And that's equivalent to one mole of NaCl.

00:21:06.690 --> 00:21:10.500
Now, after we write that, we are
going, we notice that all of our units

00:21:10.550 --> 00:21:12.610
cancel, which is really good for us.

00:21:12.650 --> 00:21:13.940
We want that to happen.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:17.240
So that way it ends up putting
it all in the correct units.

00:21:17.895 --> 00:21:21.755
So now that we have that down,
we can see that, okay, that's

00:21:21.755 --> 00:21:24.325
going to be equivalent to 0.

00:21:24.465 --> 00:21:24.845
015366

00:21:28.775 --> 00:21:31.245
moles of NaCl.

00:21:32.145 --> 00:21:35.164
Now for that, what we are
going to now do is divide that

00:21:35.204 --> 00:21:38.325
by the liters of our solvent.

00:21:39.085 --> 00:21:43.605
So, up above, we see that
we have 525 milliliters.

00:21:43.939 --> 00:21:50.180
So to convert that to liters, we'll
divide that number by 1000, making it 0.

00:21:50.320 --> 00:21:51.190
525.

00:21:52.635 --> 00:21:57.345
If we were to finish this, so what we
will do is we will take this number,

00:21:58.155 --> 00:22:03.695
we'll copy it, divide this by 0.

00:22:03.695 --> 00:22:06.365
525 liters,

00:22:09.545 --> 00:22:16.824
and what we are going
to get in return is 0.

00:22:16.825 --> 00:22:18.745
0293 molarity.

00:22:19.385 --> 00:22:22.965
Now, this is a very,
very small concentration.

00:22:23.555 --> 00:22:29.590
So when you have smaller concentrations,
Usually in introductory chem,

00:22:29.590 --> 00:22:33.520
